      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There was a significant difference in occurrence of coronary hearth disease and arterial hypertension occurrence in the sample of 16,345 patients living in northeast part of Slovak republic near Polish frontier versus to the viticulture regions of Nove Zamky, Sturovo in favour of villages in Bardejov region. Another difference was that 80 years and older respondents live significantly more frequently in south Slovakian viticulture villages."},
